{
 "_about": "\"What is this test?\" links (#163): for a lab, a reputable plain-language page about the test itself, what it measures and why it's done, never what a result means. Labs, the heatmap, the Overview tiles and the drawer's results link a lab to the page that lists it, by the series' LOINC code first, then by its name. Each page's labs are LOINC codes (lab-aliases.json or condition-presets.json's labs table names most; their names and spellings match too) or lab-aliases.json's names for labs it has no code for; aka adds spellings for a test neither file names. A lab with no page here has no link. The browser opens the page; the server contacts nothing. CONTRIBUTING.md says how to add a page; tests/test_lab_test_pages.py checks this file.",
